      "cooked": "<p>SSH does the following:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>The server sends its public host key.</li>\n<li>SSH checks the file <code>~/.ssh/known_hosts</code>.</li>\n<li>It looks for the stored host key for that server.</li>\n<li>It compares the stored key with the key received from the server.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>If they do not match, SSH shows host identification changed.</p>\n<p>Possible reasons</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Server was rebuilt/reinstalled</li>\n<li>Man-in-the-middle attack - Someone intercepting the connection.</li>\n<li>Admin manually regenerated SSH host keys</li>\n<li>Connecting to a different machine → pointing to another server</li>\n</ol>",
